<article class="ws-sheet">
<header class="ws-head"><p class="ws-kicker">Worksheet &middot; Songs in History</p><h1 class="ws-title">Worksheet: Songs of the world since 1945</h1><p class="ws-lede">A worksheet on 47 songs of the world since 1945 in Songs in History: when and where they were made, what they say and how they sound.</p><p class="ws-who" aria-hidden="true"><span>Name</span><span>Class</span><span>Date</span></p><p class="ws-tools"><button type="button" class="ws-print" data-key="0">Print the worksheet</button><button type="button" class="ws-print" data-key="1">Print with the answers</button><a href="/songs/?e=postwar">Open the songs &rarr;</a></p></header>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">1</span>Put the songs in order</h2><p class="ws-how">Number the songs from 1 (the oldest) to 6 (the newest).</p><ul class="ws-order"><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Cucurrucucú paloma</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Tian Mi Mi</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Kangding Love Song</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Wind of Change</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Imagine</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Oh Uganda, Land of Beauty</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">2</span>Where was each song made?</h2><p class="ws-how">Write the number of the right place next to each song. Their pages will help.</p><div class="ws-match"><ol class="ws-ma" type="A"><li>Cherifian Anthem</li><li>Wallah Zaman, Ya Silahi</li><li>Blowin' in the Wind</li><li>Arise, O Compatriots</li><li>Redemption Song</li><li>Kangding Love Song</li></ol><ol class="ws-mb"><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>Jamaica</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>Morocco</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>Kangding, Sichuan, China</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>Egypt</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>New York City, United States</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>Nigeria</li></ol></div></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">3</span>Think and discuss</h2><ol class="ws-qs"><li><p>Read the words of <b>Senzeni Na?</b> on its page (in English if they are in another language). What is the song about, and who might have sung it?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>Choose one song and listen to its performance. Which instruments or voices do you hear, and how does the music fit the words?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>Songs travel: find a song on these pages that was sung far from where it was made, or that gave its tune to another song. How did it travel?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li></ol></section>
<p class="ws-src">From The Epoch Institute: the-epoch-institute.org/songs/?e=postwar. Free to print and copy for use in class.</p>
<details class="ws-key" id="answers"><summary>Answer key</summary><div class="ws-key-b"><p class="ws-key-t">Answer key: Worksheet: Songs of the world since 1945</p><section><h2><span class="ws-n">1</span>Put the songs in order</h2><ol class="ws-key-list"><li>Kangding Love Song <span>1946</span></li><li>Cucurrucucú paloma <span>1954</span></li><li>Oh Uganda, Land of Beauty <span>1962</span></li><li>Imagine <span>1971</span></li><li>Tian Mi Mi <span>1979</span></li><li>Wind of Change <span>1990</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">2</span>Where was each song made?</h2><ol class="ws-key-list" type="A"><li>Cherifian Anthem <span>2: Morocco</span></li><li>Wallah Zaman, Ya Silahi <span>4: Egypt</span></li><li>Blowin' in the Wind <span>5: New York City, United States</span></li><li>Arise, O Compatriots <span>6: Nigeria</span></li><li>Redemption Song <span>1: Jamaica</span></li><li>Kangding Love Song <span>3: Kangding, Sichuan, China</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">3</span>Think and discuss</h2><p class="ws-key-note">Open questions: answers will vary. Good answers quote the song pages.</p></section></div></details>
